1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:05,190
Robbie, this new Walkman is absolutely wonderful.

2
00:00:05,190 --> 00:00:09,200
Richard and Marilyn bought it for me for my birthday.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,390
They're so thoughtful.

4
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:16,600
You are very lucky, Robbie, to have such a nice family.

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,670
Is something wrong, Alexandra?

6
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:21,040
No, nothing.

7
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,480
Yes, there is.

8
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,620
I can tell.

9
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:26,700
What's the matter?

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,270
Come on, you can tell me.

11
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:30,940
What's up?

12
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:33,270
I don't know.

13
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:37,270
Something's wrong.

14
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:42,460
OK, let's talk.

15
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:46,300
I received a letter from my parents this morning.

16
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,330
Did they write some bad news?

17
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:50,250
No.

18
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,350
Well, then why are you so sad?

19
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:53,980
I miss them.

20
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:56,680
I miss them very much.

21
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:59,640
I'm sorry, Alexandra.

22
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:03,910
But I understand.

23
00:01:03,910 --> 00:01:06,350
The Molinas treat me so nicely,

24
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:11,680
and I love being with your family so much ...

25
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,250
but when I received the letter

26
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:17,350
with photographs of my family, I cried.

27
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:19,890
I cried because I miss them all.

28
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:21,920
You really miss your family, don't you?

29
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:27,360
Yes. I know I must seem silly.

30
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:30,070
It's not like I have nobody.

31
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,230
I like the Molinas very much,

32
00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:39,180
and they're so kind to me.

33
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,720
Hey, why don't we go out

34
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,520
for a cheeseburger and french fries?

35
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,490
That'll cheer you up.

36
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:47,660
And you can use my Walkman.

37
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:50,420
That's a good idea.

38
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,560
But if we go out,

39
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,640
please don't complain

40
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:58,610
about your math teacher or your math homework.

41
00:01:58,610 --> 00:01:59,920
I want to have fun.

42
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,700
So do I.

43
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,060
I have to turn off the lights,

44
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,740
or else my father will get really angry.

45
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:09,170
He says I never turn them out when I leave.

46
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:14,910
If they come home and they're on ...

47
00:02:14,910 --> 00:02:16,240
Do you hear something?

48
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:16,660
Yes.

49
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:19,120
What was that?

50
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:21,820
It sounded like a dog barking.

51
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:24,200
It sounded like a dog barking right here.

52
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:28,440
Yeah.

53
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,590
A dog!

54
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:33,620
A springer spaniel!

55
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:34,260
Come on in!

56
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:36,100
Make yourself at home.

57
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:39,740
Oh, you poor little thing.

58
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:48,980
Come on.

59
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,190
Poor baby.

60
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:56,970
Where did you come from?

61
00:02:56,970 --> 00:02:58,670
Her name's Gemma,

62
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:02,080
and she belongs to Mr. and Mrs. Levinson.

63
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,180
There's a phone number --

64
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:09,330
five five five ... eight four four eight.

65
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:11,670
Robbie, maybe you should call them

66
00:03:11,670 --> 00:03:15,060
and tell the Levinsons we have their cute little spaniel.

67
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:17,040
I've always wanted a springer spaniel.

68
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:35,750
She's so cute.

69
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:42,040
The number you are calling -- 555-8448 --

70
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:46,830
is no longer in service.

71
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:51,420
The number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:54,010
Oh, you poor, poor baby.

73
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:56,330
You've lost your family.

74
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:57,140
We'll find them.

75
00:03:57,140 --> 00:04:00,140
Don't worry, Alexandra.
